1
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:04,090
Hi. In this video,
we're going to talk about

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:06,600
this section — the Setting Panel.

3
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:19,560
Simply put, this is where we control
RiskPilot's behavior and settings.

4
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:24,920
If you think of the panel itself
as the car's dashboard,

5
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:30,120
this part is the engine —
and it holds a lot of settings.

6
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:45,070
I'm not going to rush through
every option one after another,

7
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:49,390
because there are a lot of settings;
explaining them all at once

8
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:52,960
would be more confusing and tiring
than useful.

9
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:55,490
So I've split this section up,

10
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:59,190
and we'll make a separate
video for each part.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,710
To give you the headlines:
the appearance settings,

12
00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:24,890
and the panel size
relative to the chart and monitor.

13
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:36,620
The On Chart section
is very important — very important —

14
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:42,660
and it relates directly to Presets,
our pre-configured settings.

15
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:48,240
And as you can see, in Manual
we can adjust settings directly.

16
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:03,380
Here, On Chart is clearly connected
to this part — Presets —

17
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:05,990
which is set up and saved once.

18
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:18,320
Here we have Guards — extremely
useful for prop-challenge accounts.

19
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:24,140
We can control our daily loss,
then set and lock our spread

20
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:28,490
at a specific level, and limit
the number of trades per day

21
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:30,950
to avoid overtrading.

22
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,030
We have ATM, which is very efficient
and can implement an excellent system.

23
00:02:57,130 --> 00:02:59,670
There's the ATR section, and so on.

24
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,860
There's the PRO section
you're looking at,

25
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,870
and the Journal section.

26
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,970
And the remaining items
you're seeing here —

27
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:26,990
each has its own video.

28
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:35,240
Watching each one can be useful,
depending on your strategy.

29
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:38,530
You can implement these smart models
and trade cleanly —

30
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:42,420
the trader simply
configures everything once.

31
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,070
Based on their own strategy
and the plans they have in mind,

32
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:03,080
they set it up once
and know these settings won't change.

33
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:08,780
For fast scalping entries, it's
extremely fast and effective —

34
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:13,260
for scalpers and even fast scalpers —

35
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:18,620
since they can use the panel settings
and enter through Manual Position.

36
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:22,780
It takes the guesswork away:
how much can I risk now,

37
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:27,470
and with what percentage
or dollar amount have I entered?

38
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:37,900
Our balance isn't always round,
so we'd know exactly what size to enter

39
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:41,790
and where to exit. Often we have
to sit down and calculate

40
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:45,440
what percentage we're risking,
and how much we're up or in drawdown.

41
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:50,650
That's just a small part of what
this expert advisor can do.

42
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:58,740
It can be calculated once,
saved in the settings,

43
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:03,490
and then the trader can focus
on what matters, not such calculations.

44
00:05:20,430 --> 00:05:23,120
Thanks for your time. Good luck.
